      "id": 1795020635501.2078,
      "question": "<div style='max-width:560px;color:currentColor;margin:0 auto;'><svg viewBox='0 0 560 480' width='100%' style='display:block;max-width:520px;overflow:visible;'><polygon points='120,380 420,380 420,280 295,280 295,130 120,130' fill='rgba(128,128,128,0.15)' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='2.6' stroke-linejoin='round'/><path d='M 120 360 L 140 360 L 140 380' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.8' stroke-linejoin='round'/><path d='M 420 360 L 400 360 L 400 380' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.8' stroke-linejoin='round'/><path d='M 295 150 L 275 150 L 275 130' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.8' stroke-linejoin='round'/><path d='M 120 150 L 140 150 L 140 130' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.8' stroke-linejoin='round'/><path d='M 295 280 L 275 280 L 275 260' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.8' stroke-linejoin='round'/><path d='M 420 280 L 400 280 L 400 260' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.8' stroke-linejoin='round'/><text x='358' y='268' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='22' font-weight='700' fill='currentColor'>5 cm</text><text x='282' y='210' text-anchor='end' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='22' font-weight='700' fill='currentColor'>6 cm</text><text x='207' y='118' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='22' font-weight='700' fill='currentColor'>7 cm</text><text x='438' y='335' text-anchor='start' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='22' font-weight='700' fill='currentColor'>4 cm</text></svg></div><br>The shape below is drawn with straight lines only, and all its angles are right angles. Calculate the perimeter of the shape.",
      "options": [
        "44 cm",
        "40 cm",
        "34 cm",
        "32 cm"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "explanation": "<b>Step 1: Deduce the missing outer edges</b><br>Because all angles are right angles, opposite outer edges must match the total lengths of the shorter segments parallel to them.<br>• The total left vertical edge = inner vertical (6 cm) + right vertical (4 cm) = <b>10 cm</b>.<br>• The total bottom horizontal edge = top horizontal (7 cm) + inner horizontal (5 cm) = <b>12 cm</b>.<br><br><b>Step 2: Add all the outer sides together</b><br>Perimeter = Top (7) + Right (4) + Inner Horizontal (5) + Inner Vertical (6) + Left (10) + Bottom (12)<br>Perimeter = <b>44 cm</b>.<br><br>• Option B (40 cm) is a trap for those who forget to add the right vertical edge (4 cm).<br>• Option C (34 cm) is a trap for those who forget to add the left vertical edge (10 cm).<br>• Option D (32 cm) is a trap for those who forget to add the bottom edge (12 cm).",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 1795020796049.654,
      "question": "<span style='display: block; margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 1.05rem;'>Solve the following simultaneous equations to find the values of x and y:</span><kbd style='display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 12px; background: rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.15); padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: none; font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 1px; color: currentColor;'>2x + 3y = 12</kbd><br><kbd style='display: inline-block; background: rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.15); padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: none; font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 1px; color: currentColor;'>x − y = 1</kbd>",
      "options": [
        "x = 3, y = 2",
        "x = 2, y = 3",
        "x = 4, y = 1",
        "x = 1, y = 4"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "explanation": "We can solve this system using the substitution method by expressing x in terms of y from the second equation.<br><br><b>Step 1: Rearrange the second equation</b><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>x − y = 1</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>x = y + 1</kbd><br><br><b>Step 2: Substitute into the first equation</b><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>2(y + 1) + 3y = 12</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>2y + 2 + 3y = 12</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>5y + 2 = 12</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>5y = 10</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>y = 2</kbd><br><br><b>Step 3: Substitute y back to find x</b><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>x = 2 + 1</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>x = 3</kbd><br><br>So the solution is <b>x = 3</b> and <b>y = 2</b>.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 1795020838660.847,
      "question": "<span style='display: block; margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 1.05rem;'>Solve the following simultaneous equations to find the values of x and y:</span><kbd style='display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 12px; background: rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.15); padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: none; font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 1px; color: currentColor;'>3x + 2y = 18</kbd><br><kbd style='display: inline-block; background: rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.15); padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: none; font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 1px; color: currentColor;'>2x − y = 5</kbd>",
      "options": [
        "x = 4, y = 3",
        "x = 3, y = 4",
        "x = 5, y = 2",
        "x = 2, y = 5"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "explanation": "We can solve this system using the elimination method by making the coefficients of y opposites.<br><br><b>Step 1: Multiply the second equation by 2</b><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>2(2x − y) = 2(5)</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>4x − 2y = 10</kbd><br><br><b>Step 2: Add the new equation to the first equation</b><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>(3x + 2y) + (4x − 2y) = 18 + 10</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>7x = 28</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>x = 4</kbd><br><br><b>Step 3: Substitute x into the second equation</b><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>2(4) − y = 5</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>8 − y = 5</kbd><br><kbd style='font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;'>y = 3</kbd><br><br>So the solution is <b>x = 4</b> and <b>y = 3</b>.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
      "id": 1795020913408.7012,
      "question": "<div style='text-align: center; margin: 30px 0;'><span style='display: inline-block; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 15vw, 9rem); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 4px; background-color: rgba(255, 215, 0, 0.25); border: 4px solid currentColor; padding: 10px 30px; border-radius: 12px; color: currentColor; line-height: 1.1; max-width: 100%; word-wrap: break-word;'>MDCCLIX</span></div><br><div style='font-size: 1.1rem; text-align: center; font-weight: 600;'>Convert the very large highlighted Roman numeral above into Arabic numerals (standard numbers).</div>",
      "options": [
        "1759",
        "1769",
        "1659",
        "1749"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "explanation": "To convert the Roman numeral <b>MDCCLIX</b> to Arabic numerals, we break it down into its individual components and add them together:<br><br>• <b>M</b> = 1000<br>• <b>D</b> = 500<br>• <b>C</b> = 100<br>• <b>C</b> = 100<br>• <b>L</b> = 50<br>• <b>IX</b> = 9 (where I before X means 10 − 1)<br><br>Adding these values together:<br>1000 + 500 + 100 + 100 + 50 + 9 = <b>1759</b>.<br><br>• Option B (1769) is a trap if you mistakenly add an extra X (10).<br>• Option C (1659) is a trap if you mistake D (500) for a C (100) or misread the hundreds.<br>• Option D (1749) is a trap if you confuse L (50) with XL (40).",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
